UID:10011130-1784106000-1784111400@njaudubon.org
SUMMARY:Natural Habitats Trolley Tour
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the charming Victorian homes and sandy beaches\, Cape May is world famous for its birdwatching\, monarch migration\, and natural history. Join Cape May Bird Observatory staff and naturalists on a trolley tour to local “natural habitats” (with exits at two spots)\, learning about the beauty\, diversity\, abundance (millions of birds\, butterflies\, and dragonflies pass through each year)\, geography\, and extensive history of this amazing spectacle. \nRelax and be entertained in the birding capital of North America! Co-sponsored by New Jersey Audubon’s Cape May Bird Observatory and the Mid-Atlantic Center for the Arts and Humanities. Tours leave from the Washington Street Mall Information Booth\, where tickets may be purchased.  For more information\, call 609-884-5404 or visit www.capemaymac.org. Preregistration required.  Family-friendly. \nCost: $25 for adults and $15 for children (ages 3-12). \nREGISTER HERE \n  \n   
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/natural-habitats-trolley-tour-2/2026-07-15/
LOCATION:Washington Street Mall Info Booth\, Washington Street Mall at Ocean Street Cape May\, NJ 08204\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Birding,Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Family Program
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/NaturalHabitatsTrollyTour_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
